# Darb — Mandatory AI Rules

Read and obey `docs/AI_ENGINEERING_GUIDE.md` (Single Source of Truth). Do not violate it unless the user explicitly overrides it.

## Product identity

Darb is a **Route-Based Carpool Platform**, NOT Uber/Careem/taxi.

- Drivers publish real routes; the route is never modified by passengers.
- Passengers select only predefined landmarks (origin/destination/existing landmarks).
- Price is proposed **after** a join request — never at ride creation by the driver.

## MVP lock

Success metric until done: **one driver + multiple passengers complete a shared ride**.

Until that end-to-end flow works, do **not** add extra features.

## AI workflow (required)

1. Analyze  
2. Plan  
3. Explain  
4. Implement (only after plan / approval when required)  
5. Verify  
6. Document  
7. **Wait** — never continue automatically into the next phase

## Architecture

Prefer Clean Architecture / DDD / SOLID / Repository / DI.

Business logic must **not** live in controllers, UI, widgets, or raw API handlers — put it in Application/Domain layers (or the nearest existing service layer while migrating).

## Ride aggregate

All rules center on **Ride**: Driver, Vehicle, Route, Landmarks, Members, Join Requests, Ratings, Notifications.

## Lifecycles

- Ride: Draft → Published → Receiving Requests → Confirmed → Started → Completed → Rated → Closed  
- Join: Requested → Price Proposed → Passenger Accepted → Confirmed (or Rejected / Cancelled)

## UI / Map

- Maps first (~60% of Ride Details)
- RTL + LTR
- No free map picking in MVP for passengers — landmarks only

## Git / DoD

- One logical change per commit (`feat|fix|refactor|docs|test|perf|build|ci`)
- Done only if: requirements, tests, docs, no duplicate logic, clean build, production-ready intent

## Forbidden

Do not delete architecture, rewrite large parts, skip tests/docs, duplicate business logic, or change public APIs without explanation and approval.
